# core.autocrlf is commonly `true` on Windows, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. Pin line endings here so the repo behaves identically on every machine
# and on the Netlify build box regardless of anyone's local git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# CRITICAL: never transform the generated word data.
#
# WordIndex (src/lib/validators/offline.ts) reads words.txt as one contiguous
# Buffer, splits it on byte 0x0A, and binary-searches with Buffer.compare. A CRLF
# checkout would leave a trailing \r on every word, so every single lookup would
# fail — and it would fail only after a clone, never on the machine that built the
# file. Mark them binary so git leaves the bytes exactly as written.
poc/data/*.txt -text
poc/data/*.tsv -text

# The avatar set is photographs; `text=auto` would detect these anyway, but the
# one file in this repo that must never be transformed is spelled out above, so
# the images are spelled out too rather than left to detection.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
